: This is a _BIG_ program.

  I compiled it on 386/33 Xenix 2.3.3 with GCC 1.40 in about three hours,
BUT, I had to do lots by hand (for some reason GCC reported that it
couldn't exec gcc-cpp because of too many options, so I run it in
verbose mode and executed gcc-cpp from command line with all the
parameters gcc tried to give it and it did well. Then I had to run gcc
itself from the command line, and.. do that to 20 or so files). Hadn't I
needed any manual compiling, it would have been in 2 hours I believe.
  I don't think 2-4 hours is too much. Many programs take long to
compile, and Nethack isn't just 'any program', it's The Nethack, it's
not small one, and it's VERY important to get compiled so a couple of
hours isn't too much :-)
